# Hypergeometric motives

* [`hgm.conductor`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Hypergeometric-motives/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_hgm___conductor_FLQQ_--statement) — Conductor of a hypergeometric motive. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: Hypergeometric motives H(A, B, t) and their ℓ-adic realisations, whose conductor exponents c\_p the knowl refers to. Roadmap: PR \#1716 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/HypergeometricMotives/README.md §5.10 Local invariants at every prime, lines 2010–2016; §5.9 Tame conductor exponents and tame local degrees, lines 1968–1987
* [`hgm.good_prime`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Hypergeometric-motives/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_hgm___good_prime_FLQQ_--statement) — Primes of good and bad reduction of a hypergeometric motive. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The conductor of a hypergeometric motive (hgm.conductor). Roadmap: PR \#1716 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/HypergeometricMotives/README.md §5.3 Good, tame and wild for the motive page, lines 1773–1782 (partition defined in §1.11, lines 648–656)
* [`hgm.local_discriminant`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Hypergeometric-motives/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_hgm___local_discriminant_FLQQ_--statement) — The local discriminant of a hypergeometric motive. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The characteristic polynomial of Frobenius of a hypergeometric motive at p (from its ℓ-adic realisation, or Katz's theorem that finite hypergeometric sums are Frobenius traces). Roadmap: PR \#1716 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/HypergeometricMotives/README.md §5.12 Galois group and discriminant of the Frobenius polynomial, lines 2079–2085

# Modular forms › Siegel

* [`mf.siegel.automorphic_type`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Siegel-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___siegel___automorphic_type_FLQQ_--statement) — Automorphic type. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: Automorphic representations of GSp(4) attached to Siegel newforms and Arthur's classification of the discrete spectrum into packets of types F, P, Q, B, Y, G with their L-functions. Roadmap: PR \#1180: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularityAndLanglandsExtensions/README.md §3.9 Discrete automorphic representations of GSp₄: symplectic type, general type and transfer, lines 1882–1911 (§3.26 Arthur's classification, line 2229; §3.31, line 2359)
* [`mf.siegel.lift.ikeda`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Siegel-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_mf___siegel___lift___ikeda_FLQQ_--statement) — Duke-Imamoglu-Ikeda lift. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: Ikeda's construction (Fourier coefficients through Siegel series and the Kohnen plus space, hence the Shimura correspondence) and standard L-functions of Siegel eigenforms. Roadmap: PR \#1714 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/SiegelModularForms/README.md §9.7 The Ikeda lift, lines 2707–2727

# Representations › Artin representations

* [`artin.root_number`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Representations/Artin-representations/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_artin___root_number_FLQQ_--statement) — Root number of an Artin representation. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* issues \#43, \#44: functional equation of Artin L-functions (Brauer induction, Hecke L-functions); local constants GitHub issues: [#43](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/43), [#44](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/44). Note: Missing: The meromorphic continuation and functional equation of Artin L-functions (Brauer induction, present in Tau Ceti, plus Hecke L-functions of finite-order Hecke characters with their functional equation), so that W(ρ) is the sign of Λ(s,ρ); the product of local root numbers needs the Langlands–Deligne local constants. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ClassicalArithmeticCompletion/README.md:15104

