* [`av.princ_polarizable`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Varieties-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___princ_polarizable_FLQQ_--statement) — Principally polarizable. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* polarizations: dual abelian variety, Poincaré bundle and ampleness Note: Missing: Polarisations (dual abelian variety, Poincaré bundle, ampleness); principal polarisability is then an existential, and the canonical principal polarisation of Jacobians a construction. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/JacobianChallenge/README.md:391
* [`av.theta_divisor`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Varieties-miscellaneous/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___theta_divisor_FLQQ_--statement) — Theta divisor on a principally polarized abelian variety. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* principal polarizations and the map A → A\^∨ of a divisor (dual abelian variety); Jacobians and Kummer varieties Note: Missing: Principal polarisations and the homomorphism A → A\^∨ attached to a divisor (dual abelian variety), Jacobians and Kummer varieties. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/JacobianChallenge/README.md:392

# Varieties › Modular curves

* [`modcurve.cm_discriminants`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___cm_discriminants_FLQQ_--statement) — CM points. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* X\_H with its j-map (CM points in j-fibres) and the class number one theorem (Heegner–Baker–Stark) Note: Missing: CM points as rational points of X\_H in the j-fibres over the 13 CM j-invariants (needs X\_H with its j-map) and the class number one theorem for imaginary quadratic orders that yields the list. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ImaginaryQuadraticClassNumber/README.md:146
* [`modcurve.cusps`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___cusps_FLQQ_--statement) — Cusps of a modular curve. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* the curve X\_H over ℚ with its j-map to X(1) ≅ ℙ¹ (cusps are the fibre over ∞) Note: Missing: The curve X\_H over ℚ with its j-map to X(1) ≅ ℙ¹, so that the cusps are its fibre over ∞ (the complement of Y\_H) with their Gal\_ℚ-action. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularCurves/README.md:2206
* [`modcurve.elliptic_curve_of_point`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___elliptic_curve_of_point_FLQQ_--statement) — Elliptic curve associated to a rational point. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The curve X\_H over ℚ with the moduli bijection between its non-cuspidal K-points and pairs (E, \[ι\]\_H); the display convention (list the minimal quadratic twist once) is then immediate. Roadmap: PR \#1727 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/AdelicImagesAndModularCurves/README.md §5.2 Points of X\_H and Galois images, lines 1469–1491
* [`modcurve.embedded_model`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___embedded_model_FLQQ_--statement) — Embedded model. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: X\_G over ℚ and spaces of modular forms of even weight for an open G ≤ GL₂(Ẑ) with their ℚ-structure, giving the map of X\_G to the projectivised space whose image is the embedded model. Roadmap: PR \#1726 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/CanonicalModelsAndGonality/README.md §9.4 The LMFDB model dictionary, line 1933 (also lines 142–146 and the knowl list, line 2104)
* [`modcurve.genus_minus_rank`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___genus_minus_rank_FLQQ_--statement) — Genus-rank difference. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The analytic rank of X\_H, i.e. the L-function of its Jacobian continued to the central point (X\_H, Jacobians, Eichler–Shimura); the genus half is partly formalised (adelicGenus). Roadmap: PR \#1727 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/AdelicImagesAndModularCurves/README.md §5.9 The Jacobian J\_H and its decomposition, lines 1657–1662
* [`modcurve.j_invariant_map`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___j_invariant_map_FLQQ_--statement) — \$j\$-invariant map. Difficulty: very hard, theory. *Blocked by:* the morphism X\_H → X(1) of curves over ℚ (needs X\_H and the coarse j-line) Note: Missing: The morphism X\_H → X(1) of curves over ℚ induced by H ≤ GL₂(Ẑ) (needs X\_H and the coarse j-line) and its expression as a rational function on a model. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularCurves/README.md:2136
* [`modcurve.newform_level`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___newform_level_FLQQ_--statement) — Newform level of a modular form. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The isogeny decomposition of J\_H into modular abelian varieties A\_f (X\_H, Jacobians, Eichler–Shimura); the lcm of the newform levels (HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.level, LeanBridge) is then immediate. Roadmap: PR \#1727 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/AdelicImagesAndModularCurves/README.md §5.9 The Jacobian J\_H and its decomposition, lines 1637–1656
* [`modcurve.rank`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___rank_FLQQ_--statement) — Analytic rank. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The L-function of X\_H (of its Jacobian) with analytic continuation to the central point, or the newform Galois orbits in the isogeny decomposition of J\_H (X\_H, Jacobians, Eichler–Shimura). Roadmap: PR \#1727 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/AdelicImagesAndModularCurves/README.md §5.9 The Jacobian J\_H and its decomposition, lines 1657–1659 (convention 13, line 315)
* [`modcurve.rational_points`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Modular-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_modcurve___rational_points_FLQQ_--statement) — Rational points on a modular curve. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: The curve X\_H over ℚ with its j-map, to split X\_H(ℚ) into cuspidal, CM and other points; the genus-0/genus-1/finiteness statements are theorems (Faltings), not definitions. Roadmap: PR \#1727 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/AdelicImagesAndModularCurves/README.md §5.3 CM points and cm\_discriminants, lines 1514–1531 (points against images §5.2, cusps §5.1)

# Varieties › Shimura curves

* [`shimcurve`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Shimura-curves/#--informal-preview-shimcurve--statement) — Shimura curve. Difficulty: very hard. Note: Missing: Canonical models of quaternionic Shimura curves over ℚ (Shimura–Deligne, or moduli of QM abelian surfaces) and coarse spaces of the stack quotients \[H⧵X(O;N)\^big\]; even the complex double coset space B\^×⧵(ℋ\^± × B̂\^×)/Γ(Ô,N) is not defined. Roadmap: PR \#1722 (draft): TauCetiRoadmap/QuaternionArithmetic/README.md §9.5 Subgroups H, level, index, Γ\_H, X\_H, lines 1972–1988 (knowl list lines 2386–2389)
